{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקרא וגו' אשתו חוה", :translit "vayikra v'gomer ishto chavah", :gloss "And he called… his wife Eve"} {:he "על שם שמחוה", :translit "al sheim she'meichaveh", :gloss "on account of that she causes to speak / express"} {:he "עשרה קבין שיחה ירדו לעולם ט' נטלו נשים", :translit "asarah kabin sichah yardu la'olam tish'ah netelu nashim", :gloss "ten measures of speech descended to the world, nine took women"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: name חוה read as related to חיויה / speech (שיחה)"}], :frame {:text "The name חוה (Chavah) is explained in the verse itself as mother of all living (Genesis 3:20), from the root ח-י-ה meaning life. Ba'al HaTurim connects this to a rabbinic saying about ten measures of speech descending to the world, nine taken by women (Kiddushin 49b). The link rests on reading חוה as related to חוייא, Aramaic for speech or expression.", :sources ["Genesis 3:20" "Kiddushin 49b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: name חוה read as related to חיויה / speech (שיחה)", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:21.863774200Z", :model "glm-5.2"}